  "reasoning": "The product features an indole core fused to a saturated five-membered ring at the 2,3-positions, with a cyano group located at the bridgehead carbon. Retrosynthetic disconnection of the two sigma bonds linking the saturated ring to the indole C2 and C3 positions cleanly separates the molecule into two fragments: the parent indole nucleus and a three-carbon chain containing a nitrile and two terminal halogen leaving groups. The most chemically sound precursors are indole (c1ccc2[nH]ccc2c1) and 1,3-dichloro-2-cyanopropane (N#CC(Cl)CCl). In a forward synthesis, base-mediated sequential double SN2 alkylation of the nucleophilic C2 and C3 positions of indole onto the dichloro-nitrile efficiently constructs the fused cyclopentane ring, yielding the target heterocycle.",
  "final_answer": "c1ccc2[nH]ccc2c1.N#CC(Cl)CCl"
}

